CREATED:20260924T122115Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T122115Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_317023564@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261031T052746Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T170000
SUMMARY:Lost Libraries of the Ancient World (LECTURES - 5TH ANNIVERSARY 2N
 D DATE)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\n**A second date has been added as there are 9 on the waitli
 st for the Saturday October 24 lecture! If you are planning to take in thi
 s lecture\, get your spots early. See you then!**\n\nWe have an amazing "L
 ecture on the Go" series for 2026/2027. New topics and fascinating stories
  abound! Join me\, and uncover the world and keep active\, warm and cool d
 uring the winter and summer months!\n\nI started this walking classroom wh
 en we were under that horrible cloud called Covid. This series was popular
  and helped people get back into society and life. The first Lecture on th
 e Go was **Walking North America** and that was in October of 2021. Hard t
 o believe it's been 5 years of lectures. So I wanted to do something speci
 al to celebrate 5 years of exploration.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series 
 is open to members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's fr
 ee for those members. If you wish to attend a lecture and you are not a ye
 arly pass member then the price **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nLet's get st
 arted.\n\nWhat if some of humanity's greatest discoveries were made thousa
 nds of years ago\, and then lost forever?\n\nWhat if entire histories\, sc
 ientific breakthroughs\, literary masterpieces\, and eyewitness accounts o
 f the ancient world once existed\, only to disappear into the flames of wa
 r\, and the collapse of civilizations?\n\nJoin me for a fascinating journe
 y into the world's lost libraries\, from the legendary Library of Alexandr
 ia to the vanished collections of ancient empires whose treasures may be l
 ost forever.\n\nAt the heart\, stands the Library of Alexandria\, the most
  famous library in history. Founded over two thousand years ago\, it sough
 t to gather all the knowledge of the known world. Scholars from across the
  Mediterranean came to study astronomy\, mathematics\, geography\, medicin
 e\, philosophy\, and literature. Yet one of history's greatest mysteries r
 emains: what happened to this remarkable institution\, and what priceless 
 knowledge disappeared with it?\n\nWas it destroyed in a single catastrophe
 \, or did it slowly fade away over centuries from neglect?\n\nBeyond Alexa
 ndria\, we will explore a forgotten world of lost libraries and vanished c
 ollections stretching from Mesopotamia and ancient Egypt to medieval Europ
 e\, Baghdad\, and China. Discover the remarkable stories of librarians\, s
 cholars\, explorers\, and rulers who dedicated their lives to preserving k
 nowledge.\n\nWe will encounter lost books\, missing histories\, ancient sc
 ientific works\, and literary treasures that survive today only as fragmen
 ts.\nThis lecture is an exploration of one of history's most compelling qu
 estions: What have we forgotten?\n\nAnd how libraries shaped civilization 
 and why their loss continues to fascinate us centuries later. Whether you 
 are a lover of history\, literature\, archaeology\, or simply enjoy a good
  mystery\, this special Lecture on the Go will leave you wondering. What s
 ecrets of the past may still lie hidden\, just waiting to be rediscovered?
  Fascinating indeed!\n\nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\\*Philosop
 hy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (2027)\n\\*Philo
 sophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (20
 27)\nLegacy of Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North Amer
 ica - (September 2027)\n\nSo book your plans now!\n\nThis event is for all
  levels and walkers\, there are a few steps here and there to navigate\, b
 ut mostly on one level. This event in a non-walking event.\n\nThe lecture 
 begins on the steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay Street
  and Queen Street West\, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per person\, bu
 t **free with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please e-tra
 nsfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-t
 ransfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/317023
 564/
