CREATED:20261017T124036Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T124036Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315328327@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261031T052746Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T140000
SUMMARY:THE LIFE AND TIMES OF JANE FRANKLIN  (LECTURES)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\n**Toronto History Walks is currently working on bringing Le
 ctures on the Go to a permanent home for 2027. I will continue to update t
 his site for information as to the venue. But for now we will still meet o
 n the steps of Old City Hall until further notice.**\n\n**This is the last
  Lecture on the Go for 2026!**\n\nWe have an amazing "Lecture on the Go" s
 eries for 2027. New topics and fascinating stories abound! Join us and lea
 rn about the world and keep active and warm and cool during the winter and
  summer months!\n\nI started this walking classroom when we were under tha
 t horrible cloud called Covid. This series was popular and helped people g
 et back into society and life.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series is open t
 o members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's free for th
 ose members. If you wish to attend a lecture and you are not a yearly pass
  member then the price **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nJane Franklin was a p
 rominent 19th-century British woman known for her remarkable energy\, and 
 influence\, in exploration and colonial affairs during the Victorian era.\
 n\nShe is best remembered as the wife of John Franklin\, the Royal Navy of
 ficer who led the ill-fated Franklin Expedition. After her husband disappe
 ared in the Arctic in 1847\, Jane Franklin became one of the most determin
 ed figures in the search for him. She funded expeditions\, and lobbied the
  British government. She mobilized public attention for decades in an effo
 rt to uncover his fate and learn the truth.\n\nBut she wasn’t only defin
 ed by that search. Jane Franklin was also a widely travelled and intellect
 ually curious woman who visited places like Tasmania (then Van Diemen’s 
 Land)\, Greece\, the Middle East\, and Russia.\n\nShe also supported educa
 tion\, and science\, often working behind the scenes to influence institut
 ions like the Royal Geographical Society. You could say she became a kind 
 of unofficial power broker in British exploration.\n\nIn this lecture\, we
 ’ll explore the life and times of Jane Franklin. in the new biography se
 ries of timely women and men who made the world.\n\nUpcoming topics in the
  2027 series:\n\n\\*Philosophy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe
  to Kant! - (January 2027)\n\\*Philosophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nW
 orld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (January 2027)\nLegacy of Triangle: How a
  New York Factory Scandal changed North America - (February 2027)\nThe His
 tory of Masculinity from the Industrial Revolution to the 21st Century! (M
 arch 2027)\n\n**So book your plans now!**\n\nThis event is for all levels 
 and walkers\, there are a few steps here and there to navigate\, but mostl
 y on one level. This event in a non-walking event.\n\nThe lecture begins o
 n the steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay Street and Que
 en Street West\, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per person\, but **free
  with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please e-transfer th
 e ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer 
 to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
